[{"id":"VRCE-1-43-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":1,"english":"Then having arrived at the Ocean, the king wending in Ganga's wake, entered underneath the Earth, at that spot where those (sons of Sagara) had been reduced to ashes. And, O Rāma, on the ashes being washed by the waters of Gangā, Brahmā, the lord of all creatures thus spoke to the monarch.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.983,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"79b2d2c00883059aa48b7b13c8f44bde87f190091034629bdf79efc78f7ab069","compact":"09068eac771658e2c6da3393ed0993c6a915aa468c34c58fc357bfe4f33b7b8b","nasal":"e22fbae40562da05e38f2079c546056ac0e0935eb74a5d3f16cb300bacc220b6"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":2,"english":"Then having arrived at the Ocean, the king wending in Ganga's wake, entered underneath the Earth, at that spot where those (sons of Sagara) had been reduced to ashes. And, O Rāma, on the ashes being washed by the waters of Gangā, Brahmā, the lord of all creatures thus spoke to the monarch.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1491ba942f96a96d746e5249215bb273df1112ef7212752dd4e5004b0b5bab46","compact":"766b8ae684a89c15d3bf6db1aab2e5da3dc001534631c3fbc6c2adb18cd8b8a9","nasal":"d35412a277ab5f5a454b1b05ab67abf009a0ec4be64250a18d84c3fad9723afc"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":3,"english":"O most puissant of men, the sixty thousand sons of the high-souled Sagara have been delivered and they have ascended heaven like to celestials themselves.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d7f1374d44f5a20c3ea78874ccf17208d8ebf7cd44bfec0a5f5131a8c0b969fb","compact":"16ba932c69be244b23cfba1c135f4a903a41b07011f212d2e9623de9ade8fb4a","nasal":"16ba932c69be244b23cfba1c135f4a903a41b07011f212d2e9623de9ade8fb4a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":4,"english":"O lord of earth, as long as the waters of the ocean shall endure in the world. Sagara's sons shall reside in heaven like to celestials.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.704,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f9766b482b7028b6ba95470c7a02a871629ba21b06cf18ed2ac0efd0270b3629","compact":"8d45329e820488b1f6e5865ba9c51787c0bad4a20f02a65f1a57acb09d8eebf3","nasal":"9be3a46a268848a69fe3676e329ab59f22f1f525f8717bcc96c97568f5157d6d"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":5,"english":"This Gangā shall become your eldest daughter; and she shall attain celebrity among all, being called after your name.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bd91bb0202b568805da7daf3a2e17592b2416d6547ff84131057f4071d3e128e","compact":"185de8f1feb44e782fd2f9163441ee2fbf7dabdc7419ead1d9dbebe4e9fdfb40","nasal":"177a22a3459db206f05c35d05a4f74d6d20c0fcf7b57003ee74bacf5b88ee3ce"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":6,"english":"And Gangā is called both Tripathagã and Bhăgirathi. And she is know as Tripathagā, is consequence of her proceeding in three directions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.717,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3fb00d85e406f568174ec06a78de9a8782c5b2cc7d731ca8fa69949e032b7bfd","compact":"f27106ddd874edced4d873fc8f20ce26c46a17166a3bae1ce691a9d1795d14ea","nasal":"75958ae1cf26fadc0e864f2cc81867efef699f5ce29dd057712d770e3161ec88"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":7,"english":"Do you now, O lord of men, her offer oblations of water to your grand-sires, and thereby, O king, make good your promise.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8a3d9a9348d8f85c18496085e1ed6135b6a3cff8714b74ec253a39ae333416f0","compact":"7d31094a4596e529f4f332578c231768c1e634b65598cc9eda26ef4e385527a9","nasal":"7d31094a4596e529f4f332578c231768c1e634b65598cc9eda26ef4e385527a9"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":8,"english":"O king, that foremost of righteous ones, your ancestor of exceeding renown, had failed to attain his desire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9991fc29aa1af025005b9a124cee07a62cc2dcaad35ec607d2e4facff939210c","compact":"c1649fb6db7ce60a20ceb98f05b511afd39e958c5face2e2cdef81eba6c1d166","nasal":"c1649fb6db7ce60a20ceb98f05b511afd39e958c5face2e2cdef81eba6c1d166"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":9,"english":"O child Ansumat likewise unparalleled in the worlds in energy, had failed in realising his cherished promise of bringing down Gangā.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.71,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fce79169f040fbd58a3e0c94387fd73babdb0b609e7916f596878986d76031d6","compact":"9d77d834e60a0a84ccd498c860ee5f2134402d22c28198787eade7bcf0b7e661","nasal":"567a89becedb39a0186d114f68f38ddc2cac6f77971ed23fe8d860cd107cbf9f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":10,"english":"O child Ansumat likewise unparalleled in the worlds in energy, had failed in realising his cherished promise of bringing down Gangā.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"38686b9b71242179588fc85bc0429815c08dbbe520473717863bdf849cc79bcd","compact":"9879bd1e3eaf49ac72b031a277077f8c4d64cf04295d30f2ca34ee958d050bb6","nasal":"9879bd1e3eaf49ac72b031a277077f8c4d64cf04295d30f2ca34ee958d050bb6"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":11,"english":"Then again that royal saint, crowned with qualities; of austerities like to mine, ever abiding by his Ksatriya duties, even Dilipa's self, your exceedingly puissant sire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.842,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d8f4719be392606c876e228065237a3c376c86daae5a5162005bef469b6fed2c","compact":"97a826e64a4d1e595832a8f51ab952a569d3e5e19360fb927a09bd0135bc58cc","nasal":"666f0aa2c8a1774127671791d08a9cc7f4fc0a1cde7f4004be38fb8e06d5a821"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":12,"english":"O eminently righteous one, had failed in bringing down Gangā according to his cherished resolve, O sinless one. And now, O foremost of men, that promise having been fulfilled by you, you shall attain signal glory in the world by the common consent of all.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.917,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"01038980a031dd5fd1d62911ef5bd04471502e7a0e5c48aeb4bd58f1fbc2f6b5","compact":"4d229aca61c4fc8712fdce306c8613b0a15c584da354eaf382e572bafacfdbf8","nasal":"a225fc7be811e3d4d93e35b0e4a4f0bcb0fa8ac36ef1f6be59d4101dddd7dd60"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":13,"english":"And, O vanquisher of your foes, having brought about Ganga's dissension, you shall from this act of your also attain the regions of Brahma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.982,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"06a840acd4f9e6c337a674e96d3990f7bdc76890766c2ce096ae3f722e3b17c9","compact":"c12bae38b4869a30067c49863df55652b61995af467407db38f2be67c114a06d","nasal":"6ebd67ea6c0fdadf91fa51b16ffcd3601e1413a4237f6fc91fdb9234c34d27e7"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":14,"english":"Do you, O best of me, lave thyself in these waters worthy of the pious, O prime of men, and thereby become purified, and attain sanctity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.763,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"