 men ruled his kingdom.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.911,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eaea36de41ceed8e398f5e7cfe55da2cc83c89219b94c899638714a4a8f7391d","compact":"a94e5413ab8a83db3c3cbc851be8a374d76b5043afa49cdb623e6bc674085f1f","nasal":"a94e5413ab8a83db3c3cbc851be8a374d76b5043afa49cdb623e6bc674085f1f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":18,"english":"The royal saint king Bhagiratha also of high fame having performed his ablutions and purified himself, and duly and in proper order offered oblations of water to the sons of Sagara, entered his capital. And attaining exceeding prosperity, that foremost of men ruled his kingdom. O descendant of Raghu, having him as their sovereign, the people rejoiced greatly; and with their griefs removed and prosperity secured, they lived in peace of mind.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.598,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-15","DUTT-1-44-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"60dd34f0b0dfa6366de1ef72b4963e21ca272cace47753042e62540e2e775b6b","compact":"e144b9fb8b4539c8e2f63ae1d17cbdb0a0c52fccd219bf6dc5a4f7774729d328","nasal":"e144b9fb8b4539c8e2f63ae1d17cbdb0a0c52fccd219bf6dc5a4f7774729d328"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-43-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":43,"verse":19,"english":"Thus, O Rama, have I defailed to you the history of Gangā. Auspiciousness may you obtain! Good betide you, the evening draw nigh.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-44-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1043019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_